# CATALOGUE_SCHEMA_FLATTEN.todo
# Sprint Execution File — Catalogue Schema Flattening
# Created: 2026-03-26
# Risk Gate: Zero breakage on frontend Virtual File System
#
# Input State:
#   - catalogueType.ts (singleton document wrapping a nested array)
#   - catalogueItemType.ts (object type with recursive inline children)
#   - Singleton doc _id:"catalogue" holding entire tree as deeply nested objects
#   - Products reference catalogue nodes via catalogueLocationKeys (stores _key values)
#
# Target State:
#   - catalogueItem as a flat, independent document type (type: "document")
#   - Each node is its own Sanity document with _id = old _key (preserves product references)
#   - children modeled as references to other catalogueItem documents
#   - Singleton wrapper (catalogueType) removed entirely
#   - catalogue-index.json output format identical (zero frontend breakage)

---

## Global Directives

- Final code output must contain ZERO comments.
- Every commit must follow the taxonomy: A (Forward progress), B (Critical bug fix), C (Refactor), D (Configuration), E (Polish).
- No file may be deleted until its replacement is verified working.
- All changes to `catalogue-index.json` happen through `build-catalogue-index.mjs`, never manually.
- Migration MUST set each new document _id equal to the old nested node _key to preserve product catalogueLocationKeys references without touching product documents.
- The current catalogue-index.json has 3 root nodes, 8 group headers, 20 leaf links (31 total nodes). The slugToIdMap is currently empty (all roots/groups are headers, no non-header node has a slug in the current data set). The slotMetadataMap has 3 entries (root headers only — they are the only nodes with slugs). These counts are invariants for migration verification.

---

## Layer 1: Schema Deployment

### Scope Contract

Redefine `catalogueItem` from `type: "object"` to `type: "document"`, making each catalogue node an independent, queryable Sanity document. Remove the singleton `catalogueType` wrapper entirely. Retain all existing fields (`title`, `type`, `slug`, `icon`) required by the build-catalogue-index pre-compute script. Transform `children` from inline nested objects to an array of references. Add `sortOrder` field for deterministic sibling ordering.

**Files Modified:**
- `sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueItemType.ts` — object → document, children → references, add sortOrder
- `sanity/schemaTypes/index.ts` — remove catalogueType import and registration
- `sanity/structure.ts` — replace singleton catalogue entry with catalogueItem document list

**Files Removed (deferred to Layer 5):**
- `sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueType.ts` — singleton wrapper (marked for deletion, not deleted here)

**Invariant:**
- The field names `title`, `type`, `slug`, `icon` must remain exactly as-is on the new document type.

### DoD

- [ ] 1.1 — In `sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueItemType.ts`: change `type: "object"` to `type: "document"`. Change `children` field from `of: [{ type: "catalogueItem" }]` to `of: [{ type: "reference", to: [{ type: "catalogueItem" }] }]`. Add new field `sortOrder` of type `number` with `initialValue: 0` after the `icon` field. Remove the commented-out `preview` block. Add a `preview` block that selects `title` and `type`, and returns `{ title, subtitle: type === "header" ? "Group" : "Link" }`.
  - Difficulty: 3 - C(sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueItemType.ts): promote catalogueItem to document type with reference children — closes DoD item 1.1

- [ ] 1.2 — In `sanity/schemaTypes/index.ts`: remove the import of `catalogueType` from `"./catalogueType"` (line 4). Remove `catalogueType` from the `types` array (line 9). Leave all other imports and registrations untouched.
  - Difficulty: 1 - C(sanity/schemaTypes/index.ts): deregister singleton catalogueType — closes DoD item 1.2

- [ ] 1.3 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: replace the `S.listItem().title("Catalogue").child(S.document().schemaType("catalogue").documentId("catalogue").title("Catalogue"))` block (lines 9-16) with `S.documentTypeListItem("catalogueItem").title("Catalogue")`. Update the filter array on line 27 to exclude `"catalogueItem"` instead of `"catalogue"`: `!["catalogueItem", "homepage"]`.
  - Difficulty: 2 - C(sanity/structure.ts): show catalogueItem document list instead of singleton — closes DoD item 1.3

### Verification — Layer 1

