## Layer 2: Data Migration Script

### Scope Contract

Create a one-time migration script `scripts/migrate-catalogue-to-flat.mjs` that reads the existing singleton tree from Sanity Content Lake and creates one independent `catalogueItem` document per node. Each document's `_id` MUST equal the old node's `_key` to preserve all existing product `catalogueLocationKeys` references without modifying product documents. Children are stored as Sanity reference objects. Sort order reflects original array position. The old singleton document is NOT deleted by this script.

**Files Created:**
- `scripts/migrate-catalogue-to-flat.mjs` — one-time migration script

**Critical Invariant:**
- `newDoc._id === oldNode._key` for every node in the tree. This is the zero-breakage guarantee for product `catalogueLocationKeys`.

### DoD

- [ ] 2.1 — Create `scripts/migrate-catalogue-to-flat.mjs`. The script must:
  (a) Load env vars and create a Sanity client (same pattern as seed-catalogue.mjs).
  (b) Fetch the old singleton: `*[_id == "catalogue"][0].catalogue`.
  (c) Recursively walk the tree. For each node, produce a document object:
      ```
      {
        _id:        node._key,
        _type:      "catalogueItem",
        title:      node.title,
        type:       node.type,
        slug:       node.slug || undefined,
        icon:       node.icon || undefined,
        sortOrder:  <index within parent array>,
        children:   (node.children || []).map(child => ({
                      _type: "reference",
                      _ref:  child._key,
                      _key:  child._key
                    }))
      }
      ```
  (d) Collect ALL document objects into a flat array.
  (e) Use a Sanity transaction (`client.transaction()`) with `createOrReplace` for each document.
  (f) Commit the transaction.
  (g) Print summary: total documents created, root count, group count, leaf count.
  - Difficulty: 5 - A(scripts/migrate-catalogue-to-flat.mjs): create flat migration script — closes DoD item 2.1

- [ ] 2.2 — Execute the migration script: `node scripts/migrate-catalogue-to-flat.mjs`. Capture output. Verify console reports 31 total documents (3 roots, 8 groups, 20 leaves).
  - Difficulty: 1 - D(scripts): run migration — closes DoD item 2.2

### Verification — Layer 2

- [ ] V2.1 — Write `scripts/verify-migration.mjs`. The script must:
  (a) Fetch all: `*[_type == "catalogueItem"]`.
  (b) Assert total count === 31.
  (c) Assert exactly 3 documents have `icon` field defined (root nodes).
  (d) Assert exactly 20 documents have `type == "link"` (leaf nodes).
  (e) Assert exactly 11 documents have `type == "header"` (roots + groups).
  (f) For every document with children references, assert each `_ref` resolves to an existing document in the result set.
  (g) Fetch all `*[_type == "product"].catalogueLocationKeys` and assert every key value exists as a `_id` in the catalogueItem result set.
  (h) Print PASS/FAIL per assertion.
  - Difficulty: 5 - A(scripts/verify-migration.mjs): create migration verification script — closes DoD V2.1

- [ ] V2.2 — Run `node scripts/verify-migration.mjs`. All assertions must PASS.
  - Difficulty: 1

