## Layer 3: Pre-Compute Script Update

### Scope Contract

Update `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs` to query flat `catalogueItem` documents instead of the singleton. Reconstruct the nested tree in memory from the flat document set. Output `catalogue-index.json` with identical structure: `{ generatedAt, slugToIdMap, slotMetadataMap, tree }`. The `tree` output must use `_key` property (set to `_id` value) for backward compatibility with any consumer reading tree nodes. All URL path construction, breadcrumb generation, and metadata mapping logic must produce equivalent results.

**Files Modified:**
- `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs` — new GROQ query, tree reconstruction, _key mapping

**Output Contract (identical to current):**
- `slugToIdMap`: `Record<urlPath, documentId>` — maps URL path strings to document `_id` values (equivalent to old `_key`).
- `slotMetadataMap`: `Record<documentId, { title, url, slug, breadcrumbs, children, type }>` — maps document `_id` to metadata (same shape).
- `tree`: Array of nested node objects with `_key`, `_type`, `title`, `type`, `slug`, `icon`, `children`.

### DoD

- [ ] 3.1 — In `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`: replace the GROQ query `*[_id == "catalogue"][0].catalogue` with `*[_type == "catalogueItem"]{ _id, title, type, slug, icon, sortOrder, "childRefs": children[]._ref }`. Store result in a variable `allItems`.
  - Difficulty: 2 - C(scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs): switch to flat document query — closes DoD item 3.1

- [ ] 3.2 — In `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`: implement tree reconstruction from the flat document array. The algorithm must:
  (a) Build a lookup map: `itemById[doc._id] = doc` for every document in `allItems`.
  (b) Identify root nodes: iterate `allItems`, collect all `_id` values that appear in any document's `childRefs` into a Set `referencedIds`. Root nodes are those whose `_id` is NOT in `referencedIds`.
  (c) Sort root nodes by `sortOrder`.
  (d) Implement a recursive function `buildTreeNode(doc)` that returns:
      ```
      {
        _key:     doc._id,
        _type:    "catalogueItem",
        title:    doc.title,
        type:     doc.type,
        slug:     doc.slug || undefined,
        icon:     doc.icon || undefined,
        children: (doc.childRefs || [])
                    .map(ref => itemById[ref])
                    .filter(Boolean)
                    .sort((a, b) => (a.sortOrder || 0) - (b.sortOrder || 0))
                    .map(buildTreeNode)
      }
      ```
      Omit `slug`, `icon`, `children` keys when undefined/empty to match current output shape.
  (e) Build the full tree: `rootNodes.map(buildTreeNode)`.
  - Difficulty: 5 - A(scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs): implement tree reconstruction from flat documents — closes DoD item 3.2

- [ ] 3.3 — In `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`: replace the current `traverse(catalogue)` call with the new tree. Pass the reconstructed tree into the existing `traverse` function (which builds `slugToIdMap` and `slotMetadataMap`). Update the traverse function to use `node._key` (which is now set to the `_id` value from tree reconstruction). Set `output.tree` to the reconstructed tree.
  - Difficulty: 3 - C(scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs): integrate reconstructed tree into traverse and output — closes DoD item 3.3

### Verification — Layer 3

- [ ] V3.1 — Before running the updated script, save a copy of the current `data/catalogue-index.json` as `data/catalogue-index.pre-flatten.json`.
  - Difficulty: 1

- [ ] V3.2 — Run `node scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`. Verify:
  (a) Script completes without errors.
  (b) Output file `data/catalogue-index.json` is generated.
  (c) Top-level keys are: `generatedAt`, `slugToIdMap`, `slotMetadataMap`, `tree`.
  - Difficulty: 1

- [ ] V3.3 — Write `scripts/verify-catalogue-index.mjs`. The script must:
  (a) Load both `catalogue-index.pre-flatten.json` and the new `catalogue-index.json`.
  (b) Assert `Object.keys(newData.slugToIdMap).length === Object.keys(oldData.slugToIdMap).length`.
  (c) Assert `Object.keys(newData.slotMetadataMap).length === Object.keys(oldData.slotMetadataMap).length`.
  (d) Assert `newData.tree.length === oldData.tree.length` (3 root nodes).
  (e) For each key in old `slotMetadataMap`: assert the corresponding key in new `slotMetadataMap` has identical `title`, `slug`, `type`, and `children.length`.
  (f) Recursively count all nodes in old `tree` vs new `tree`: assert equal totals (31).
  (g) Assert every `_key` in the new tree matches a valid entry in `slotMetadataMap` (for nodes that have slugs).
  (h) Print PASS/FAIL per assertion.
  - Difficulty: 5 - A(scripts/verify-catalogue-index.mjs): create catalogue-index structural comparison script — closes DoD V3.3

- [ ] V3.4 — Run `node scripts/verify-catalogue-index.mjs`. All assertions must PASS.
  - Difficulty: 1

