Fix the TypeScript type dependency in `data/catalogue.ts` that breaks when `Catalogue` type is removed from auto-generated `sanity.types`. Delete the now-unused `catalogueType.ts` file. Delete the old singleton document from the Content Lake. Regenerate `sanity.types`. Verify the full pipeline end-to-end.

**Files Modified:**
- `data/catalogue.ts` — replace `Catalogue` type import with standalone type definition

**Files Deleted:**
- `sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueType.ts` — singleton wrapper (no longer registered, safe to delete)

